# Stacks 03YM: the quasi-coherent modules form a stack over the big fppf site

Stacks 03YM asserts that the projection `p : 𝒬𝒞oh ⟶ (Sch/S)_fppf` of Stacks 04U2 satisfies the
three conditions of Stacks 026F, which in the tree are the three fields of
`CategoryTheory.Functor.IsStack`: `p` is a fibred category, the presheaves `Mor(x, y)` of
Stacks 02ZB on each slice are sheaves, and every descent datum along a covering sieve is
effective.  All three are proved here, as `Stacks.QCoh.projection_isStack`.

Condition (1) is the existence of cartesian lifts: a lift of `f : V ⟶ U` at a quasi-coherent
module `M` on `U` is the unit `M ⟶ f_* f^* M` of the pullback–pushforward adjunction read as an
`f`-map (`moduleCartesianMap`), and it is strongly cartesian by Stacks 04U3.

Conditions (2) and (3) together are Mathlib's stack condition for the pullback pseudofunctor of
`p` (`CategoryTheory.Functor.isStack_pullbackPseudofunctor_iff`), that is, the statement that the
comparison from a fibre to the descent data of each covering family is an *equivalence*; full
faithfulness alone is condition (2) and essential surjectivity is the extra content of
condition (3).  The comparison is factored through quasi-coherent descent data on schemes in
three steps.

First the fibre of `p` over an object `U` of the big fppf site over `S` is identified with the
opposite of the category of quasi-coherent modules on the underlying scheme of `U`:
`modulesToFiber` is that comparison and `modulesToFiber_isEquivalence` is Stacks 04U3 in the form
needed here.

Second, descent data for `p` along a family of the site are identified with quasi-coherent descent
data for the underlying family of schemes: `moduleDescentFunctor` compares the fibre-wise data with
the sieve-free data of Stacks 023B read on the site, and `schemeDescentRestriction` compares the
latter with the data on schemes, the chosen pullbacks of the site being `sitePullback`.  Both
comparisons are equivalences; essential surjectivity of the second is `extendDescentData`, which
reads a datum of the site as gluing data of `CategoryTheory.Pseudofunctor.DescentData'` over the
images in schemes of the chosen pullbacks of the site (`imageDescentData`).  That construction is
carried out over a variable functor and a variable pseudofunctor and instantiated here: at the
concrete ones, identifying the fibres of the restricted pseudofunctor with those of
`AlgebraicGeometry.modulePullbackPseudofunctor` is definitional but unfolds the latter.

Third, the comparison is identified with the canonical descent functor of Stacks 023D
(`canonicalComparisonNatIso`), which is an equivalence by the two halves of Stacks 023T:
`AlgebraicGeometry.nonempty_fullyFaithful_canonicalDescentFunctor'` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.QuasicoherentDescentData.isEffective_fpqcPrecoverage`.  Both hold for an
arbitrary fpqc covering family, and an fppf covering is an fpqc covering; they are used at index
universe `u + 1`, which is where the covering families of a big fppf site live.

## Main results

* `Stacks.QCoh.projection_isStack`: **Stacks 03YM**.

## Implementation notes

`Stacks.QCoh.projection` is read off a `Stacks.QCoh.CategoryData` obtained by choice from
Stacks 04U2, so its action on arrows is only pinned up to the two identifications
`projection_obj` and `projection_map` that the data carry.  `rawProjection` below is the functor
written directly in terms of the `f`-map description of the hom-sets, `rawProjection_eq_projection`
identifies it with `Stacks.QCoh.projection`, and the whole argument is carried out for it.

Quasi-coherence of a module on a scheme `T` is named `qcohProp T`, whose *declared* type is
`ObjectProperty T.Modules` while its body is `SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent T.ringCatSheaf`.  The
two agree only after `TopCat.Sheaf` unfolds — `T.ringCatSheaf` is a
`TopCat.Sheaf RingCat T.toPresheafedSpace` and `SheafOfModules` asks for a
`Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology T) RingCat` — so a goal spelled the second way is not
type-correct at the transparency used for implicit arguments, and `simp` on such a goal makes no
progress at all.  Naming the property with the declared type performs that identification once, and
every statement below is spelled with `qcohProp`.  The same mismatch is why the comparison of
`schemeRestrictionExtendIso` is assembled from `Eq.trans` and `congrArg` instead of by `rw`: a
motive abstracting a subterm of that goal is not type-correct either.

The topology on the big fppf site over `S` is the localisation at `S` of the topology generated by
the site's chosen covering families; `bigFppfOver_topology_eq_fppf` identifies it with the topology
generated by the comparison of Mathlib's fppf precoverage along the functor to schemes, which is
the form in which `CategoryTheory.Pseudofunctor.IsStack.of_precoverage` applies.  The
identification of the chosen families with the fppf coverings of the site is
`AlgebraicGeometry.bigFppf_precoverage_eq`, and it needs the combinatorial cofinality field of
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfSite`.

